  "method": "A source-declared head binds five connected finite original-STL material-core paths. Every path has a certified radius >=0.4 mm from all original triangles, using exact point-to-original-triangle distances at <=0.04 mm spacing, a 1-Lipschitz complete-segment bound, a 1.5 mm omitted-face bounding-box lower bound, and a 1e-6 mm guard. Material side is checked by compensated long-double solid-angle winding over all original triangles. Each instance retains 13 raw original-triangle sections and 76 direct BVH all-hit cross-section rays with first root-solid and next-air intervals, face identity, tangent/coplanar records and material/air controls.",
  "limits": "Finite root-neighborhood linkage certificate only. Does not classify or exempt any morphology opening-loss polygon or original-normal short chord; those require separate source-bounded evidence and independent review. The measured tube is a certified connected >=0.8 mm core, not a claim that every local shell point or every shell face normal has >=0.8 mm thickness. No mesh was repaired, filtered, remeshed or healed.",
  "elapsed_seconds": 58.07832455635071
}
